<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia calls Australian &quot;sore loser&quot; over Games.</title>
<headline>Malaysia calls Australian &quot;sore loser&quot; over Games.</headline>
<byline>Reme Ahmad</byline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian sports officials denied on Saturday that Kuala Lumpur used &quot;the power of money&quot; to win its bid to host the 1998 Commonwealth Games, as alleged by an Australian sports official.</p>
<p>Siah Kok Chi, honorary secretary of the Olympic Council of Malaysia, said Australian Commonwealth Games Secretary-General Arthur Tunstall sounded like a &quot;sore loser&quot; for making claims he could not back with evidence.</p>
</text>
